      "file_path": "D:\\Github\\Virtual\\wyr-virtual-listing\\CLAUDE.md",
      "new_string": "**Card Copy Program** (`routes/cardCopy.js` + `services/cardCopy*.js`): a port of the `CloneCardSellerProgram` C# WinForms app. The operator pastes a client's RFID memory-bank dump (Order ID + Data A–E = Reserved/EPC/TID/User/DateTime), which is parsed (`cardCopyParser.js`) and run through TID chip identification (`cardCopyTidParser.js`). On approve, the backend recomputes a verification hash and an **AES-256-CBC encrypted `BEGIN_SELLER_DATA…END_SELLER_DATA` blob** (`cardCopyCrypto.js`) for the client to decrypt. **`cardCopyCrypto.js` must stay byte-compatible with the desktop app** — same passphrase (zero-padded to 32 bytes), AES-256-CBC/PKCS7, `base64(IV+ciphertext)` then base64 again inside the wrapper, and the same SHA-256 checksum/hash construction — or existing client programs can no longer decrypt it. `cardCopyCrypto.test.mjs` locks the round-trip and checksum. Orders are upserted by `order_id` (`cardCopyOrders.js`), replacing the desktop app's local JSON file.\n\n**Mykad Key Issuer** (`services/keyGenerator.js`): a port of a legacy WinForms \"MYR Key Issuer\" app.",
